NetworkStatsFactory: Report no statistics on a kernel without xt_qtaguid

The Echo Dot (2nd gen) and the MT8163 Echo Shows run a 4.9 kernel with
neither eBPF nor xt_qtaguid, so /proc/net/xt_qtaguid does not exist.
NetworkStatsService polls it every 30 minutes and on every network
change. Reading stats failed, the service logged a wtf ("problem reading
network stats") and DropBox wrote an entry to flash each time.

When those files are missing, report empty statistics from all three
readers: per UID (stats), per interface (iface_stat_all) and the xt
summary (iface_stat_fmt), which returned null and would crash
NetworkStatsService once the other two stopped failing first. Android's
data usage numbers were already empty on these kernels.

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/net/NetworkStatsFactory.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/net/NetworkStatsFactory.java
index 86ad0b30..766ef344 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/net/NetworkStatsFactory.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/net/NetworkStatsFactory.java
@@ -201,6 +201,13 @@ public class NetworkStatsFactory {
         final NetworkStats stats = new NetworkStats(SystemClock.elapsedRealtime(), 6);
         final NetworkStats.Entry entry = new NetworkStats.Entry();
 
+        // A kernel with neither eBPF nor xt_qtaguid has no such file. Report
+        // no interfaces instead of failing every poll.
+        if (!mStatsXtIfaceAll.exists()) {
+            StrictMode.setThreadPolicy(savedPolicy);
+            return stats;
+        }
+
         ProcFileReader reader = null;
         try {
             reader = new ProcFileReader(new FileInputStream(mStatsXtIfaceAll));
@@ -254,12 +261,16 @@ public class NetworkStatsFactory {
 
